  to  get a lot of the language in me before i  try to  read any explanations of  what the language does i prefer to  experience the language first so there's  many different ways of doing things now  speak from day one why am i speaking so  early  uh in my learning insofar as farsi is  concerned  the biggest reason is that we don't have  text to speech at link  so because both arabic and farsi  uh with their script it's sometimes  difficult to know how to pronounce the  words  so with arabic i can click on and i can  hear it in text to speech  with farsi there is no text to speech so  what i do with my tutor  oh that's point number one at point  number two i think what has dramatically  changed in my language learning is the  many stories  the many stories  i believe dramatically sped up my  learning of greek  arabic and now farsi because the stories  contain  the most common verbs  they repeat the vocabulary and the  structures within each story three times  at least  and so we get a very very soon we get a  sense of word order we get a sense of  positive you know yes nose type  sentences questions  uh all of this kind of stuff that is  typically described in grammar  explanations through this repetitive  nature of the many stories you start to  get a feel of the language so i feel  that i'm progressing more quickly than  was the case when i was learning say  russian or czech we didn't have the many  stories so that's point number one  uh point number two  having the many stories now that i have  listened to  uh the top the first 10 minute stories  in farsi i've listened to 30 times  each one of them 25 to 35 times  that gives me something to take into my  conversation with my tutor even though i  only have 350 known words  i have listened to a limited number of  these stories  so many times that i'm in a position to  at least use that vocabulary to some  extent with mistakes and whatnot  so  you know i've got this concentrated  bit of the language that we can build  our conversation around and that makes  it a  pleasant experience obviously too if  we're on skype the connection has to be  good the person the tutor has to be  pleasant all of these things are  important  where the skype connection is poor uh  then it's very difficult to have a  lesson uh also  uh if if you go in there to have a  discussion and  every third word you don't understand  and then they so then i say how do you  say this and then the tutor explains it  and of course just by hearing it  especially with a poor connection makes  no impact on me whatsoever  if the tutor sends me a list of these  words later on i can review them but  with uh taking these sort of mini  stories then i've got a sort of a  concentrated dose of the language that i  can get into discussion around  the other thing we do  which is very valuable to me is that i  read the farsi out loud because it's not  like reading spanish or reading slovak  where  basically it's written the way it's  pronounced  uh for me to get used to the arabic  writing system and get to get used to  how these words are pronounced and so  forth i find it very useful to read  say the part one of one of these many  stories then we have a discussion around  that then we go on to another one we do  two stories per session so far  now  so to get from that so that's why i'm  starting early  uh would i start early on let's say if i  started learning turkish where the  apparently the the writing system is  very fanatic would i do the same i might  so then why why do i consider it useful  to speak  because  the speaking improves my  ability to focus on what i'm listening  to and reading so in other words  the goal of the  conversation is to improve the quality  of my listening and reading  because and i would take it even further  most of what i do  is  has the goal of making my listening more  valuable because i have more time  available to listen than anything else  in my car  doing the dishes and whatever so the  reading that i do the reviewing of words  and phrases talking to my tutor reading  again on the ipad or on the computer  it's all with the goal that when i am  listening  i'm able to write to derive the maximum  benefit out of it because listening is  the main sort of production engine  production end of my language learning  so  taking all of this now back to  this comment  here about how  you know language exchange wasn't  helping a lot  i believe that  you know speaking is going to help you  if you get a lot of it in other words if  you are immersed in the language and you  are every evening or three four hours a  day speaking in the language you're  getting so much input that you're going  to improve but if you are speaking three  times a week  on some kind of language exchange that  is not going to improve you very much  if it is  an incentive motivation  it heightens your your ability to  observe the language stimulates you all  of those things are good but then the  major learning activity in my mind is  still the listening and reading  and uh so this person for example who's  on a language exchange you know that can  be very motivating  uh i want to improve for the next time i  speak to rana in in farsi so it's it's  motivating but the the the place i'm  going to improve is through my reading  and listening and  you know review after each lesson of the  words and phrases that kind of activity  which i can organize easily i don't have  to set up on a you know a time slot for  it i just get in the car and it's on  it's it's always with me  and so that's where i learn  and the role of speaking  is to  create you know to improve the quality  of your input activity unless of course  you are surrounded by the language in  which case you are getting enough input  so speaking speaking early speaking a  little bit later it depends on your  situation depends on what you like to do  but to me it's still primarily to  improve the effectiveness of your input  learning activities  so and i will go and find benny and we  will disagree over this and it's  perfectly okay to disagree on anything  nowadays it's as if we have to persuade  everybody of everything we don't we can  have an opinion someone has a different  opinion we can exchange our views we're  stimulated we agree we disagree we maybe  move our views slightly it's all good  okay thank you for listening  bye for now  [Music]  you
 

